design_snippets:
Framed envelope wire format (length-prefixed UTF-8): <len>
<json>
 where <len> is ASCII decimal of byte length of the following JSON body. Example: 102
{"envelope_type":"tool_call","id":"t-1",...}
Envelope schema example (JSON): {"envelope_type": "tool_output", "id": "t-1", "session_token": "s-abc", "seq": 3, "payload": {"mime": "application/json", "data": {...}}}
Typescript FramedStreamReader usage (pseudo):
const reader = new FramedStreamReader(response.body);
for await (const env of reader.envelopes()) {
  if (env.envelope_type === 'checkpoint') saveCheckpoint(env.session_token);
  if (env.envelope_type === 'tool_output') handleToolOutput(env);
}
Python async generator usage (pseudo):
async for env in client.stream_envelopes(req):
  if env['envelope_type'] == 'tool_call': start_local_runner(env)
  if env['envelope_type'] == 'checkpoint': await checkpoint_store.save(env['session_token'])

# resume: await client.resume_envelopes(session_token, from_seq=5)
Go channel pattern (pseudo):
streamer := client.NewEnvelopeStreamer(req)
for env := range streamer.C() {
  switch env.EnvelopeType {
  case 'tool_output': process(env)
  case 'error': log.Error(env.Message)
  }
}
// to resume: streamer.Resume(sessionToken)
